    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0480" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/99</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-25T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 25, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 13, 11 a.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d443-f1"/> Shipping Board has
                    designated you as its agent to accept the title of the German interned ships in
                    Cuba. When ships are handed over to you, convey to the Cuban Government an,
                    expression of the gratification of this Government for the generous action of
                    the Cuban Government in promptly placing at our disposal, the ships in
                    question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d443-f1" n="2" xml:id="d443-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram of July 9, 6 p.m., to the Minister, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg307">p. 307</ref>.</p>
            </note>
